# Mathematical Notation Conventions

## Core Constants

| Symbol | Definition | Numerical Value |
|--------|------------|-----------------|
| φ | Golden ratio (1+√5)/2 | 1.6180339887... |
| φ⁻¹ | 1/φ = φ-1 | 0.6180339887... |
| φ² | φ+1 | 2.6180339887... |
| φ³ | φ²+φ | 4.2360679775... |
| φ⁻³ | 1/φ³ | 0.2360679775... |

## Key Identities (Use These)

- φ² = φ + 1
- φ⁻¹ = φ - 1
- φ + φ⁻¹ = √5
- φ² + φ⁻² = 3
- φⁿ = φⁿ⁻¹ + φⁿ⁻²

## Lattice and Root Notation

| Symbol | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| Λ_E₈ | The E₈ lattice |
| α, β, γ | E₈ roots (vectors in ℝ⁸) |
| D₈ | Type D₈ roots: (±1,±1,0⁶) permutations |
| S₈ | Type S₈ roots: ½(±1)⁸ with even minus signs |

## Projection Notation

| Symbol | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| P_φ | Golden projection matrix (8×4) |
| V_phys | Physical subspace (4D) |
| V_int | Internal subspace (4D or 5D) |
| x = P_φ·α | Physical projection of root α |
| ξ = π_int(α) | Internal projection of root α |
| h(α) | Height (latitude) of projected root |

## 600-Cell Notation

| Symbol | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| H₄ | The 4D icosahedral group (order 14,400) |
| H₃ | The 3D icosahedral group (order 120) |
| R_inner | Radius of inner 600-cell (~0.7435) |
| R_outer | Radius of outer 600-cell (~1.2030) |

## Height Spectrum (Standard Values)

- h = ±2 : Poles (1 vertex each)
- h = ±φ : Icosahedral bands (12 vertices each)
- h = ±1 : Dodecahedral bands (20 vertices each)
- h = ±φ⁻¹ : Intermediate bands (12 vertices each)
- h = 0 : Equator (30 vertices)

## Physical Quantities

| Symbol | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| θ_W | Weinberg (weak mixing) angle |
| sin²θ_W | ~0.231 (observed at M_Z) |
| θ_C | Cabibbo angle (~13°) |
| Q | Koide ratio (2/3 for leptons) |
| θ₀ | Koide phase (~347° for leptons) |

## LaTeX Formatting

- Use $...$ for inline math
- Use $$...$$ for display math
- Use \varphi for φ (golden ratio)
- Use \theta_W for Weinberg angle
- Use \mathfrak{e}_8 for the E₈ Lie algebra
